Hey [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] 

Please find below answers to your question.

{quote}* Does anyone (either internally or a third party) have access to both the hashed and unhashed values?{quote}

I believe the other platforms (Uber, Heetch etc..) would have access to both values, just like we do. However, I do not believe that the recipient (Deloitte) has access to unhashed values.

{quote}* Could the hash be cross-referenced with other datasets to re-identify the driver?{quote}

I believe yes. Deloitte wants to aggregate driver’s data from all platforms to provide a consolidated view. With the hashed PHV license numbers, Deloitte will be able to consolidate drivers' activity across all platforms.

{quote}* Does the recipient of the hash have any means to associate it with the original driver information?{quote}

Not sure if the recipient will be able to identify the driver. If all they receive is data in the format we’re asked to provide, then it “isn’t possible” to know the identity of the driver, as this requires de-hashing the PHV license number .

{quote}* Will they combine it with other data that could re-identify drivers?{quote}

As stated above, the recipient will combine data from other platforms, using the hashed PHV license number which should be common to all platforms.

